{
 "esm": "1.3.0",
 "metadata": {
  "name": "cam_zm_parcel",
  "description": "CAM6 ZM deep convection, stage 2: the parcel/CAPE block (buoyan_dilute, zm_convr.F90:800-1150, with the parcel_dilute per-level laws, F90:1152-1486, and the entropy function, F90:1489-1513). Model Parcel carries the per-level closed-form laws of the buoyancy calculation - the environment saturation specific humidity qst and the moist static energies hmn/hsat (cldprp, F90:1829-1830; hmn is also the hmn_lev law of the parcel_pbl branch, F90:979, and the hmax search law of the default branch, F90:1018), the virtual temperatures tv/tpv (F90:1005-1006, 1088, 1415, 1476), the Raymond-Blyth entropy ent (F90:1489-1513), the buoyancy buoy = tpv - tv + tiedke_add for msg+1 <= k <= maxi, else 0 (F90:1088-1089; below msg+1 buoy keeps its zero initialization, F90:1006-1007; the plge600 gate of F90:1079-1080 is omitted - pl is dumped and >= 600 mb on all active rows), and the CAPE integral cape = max(0, integral over d(ln p) of rd buoy over lel < k <= maxi) (F90:1124, 1146; with num_cin = 1 the candidate selection of F90:1136-1140 collapses to lel = lelten(1) and cape = capeten(1), verified against the dumped capeten/lelten columns (cam_zm_parcel_scal.csv), so lel enters as a parameter). The launch level maxi is a parameter: it is the argmax of hmn over k >= pblt (F90:1018-1020), and argmax is not evaluable in the CLI interpreter (probed); the branch law qstp = q at the launch level (parcel_dilute, F90:1414) is carried by the qstp_launch unknown as the bare index q(maxi) (a definition, not pinned by any test). NOT expressible and carried as parameters (see README-cam-zm-parcel.md): the parcel ascent solve (ientropy, F90:1517-1632) fixes tp, qstp, tl, lcl, pl, and the internal tmix/qsmix/xsh2o; qtot = new_q is dumped (cam_zm_parcel.csv), so tpv, buoy and cape are pinned (qtot defaults to the step-18 profile, the step-18 test running on the defaults). Tests pin hmn/hsat against the dumped columns at lev {1,15,25,32} for all 15 active steps (cam_zm.csv rows (step,1,k), cam_zm_scal.csv row (step,1)), qst at lev {25,32} against the dumped cam_zm.csv qs column (also cross-pinned by hsat through hsat = cp t + grav z + rl qst), tpv at lev {25,32} and buoy at lev {15,18,25} against the dumped cam_zm_parcel.csv columns, cape against the dumped cam_zm_scal.csv cape (== capeten_1), and ent/tv at five (step, lev) states against the entropy and virtual-temperature replicas (DERIVED). Numeric tuples generated by stage1/analysis/zm_parcel_closure_tuples.py. Units: working pressures hPa, dp-free; all constants are the zm_convr_run values (cpres = 1004.64 J/(kg K), rl = 2.501e6 J/kg, rgas = 287.0423113650487 J/(kg K), eps1 = 0.6219705862045155, tfreez = 273.15 K, grav = 9.80616 m/s^2, cpliq = 4188 J/(kg K), cpwv = 1810 J/(kg K), rh2o = 461.5046398201599 J/(kg K), tiedke_add = 0.5 K, tpert = 0 K in this lane).",
  "license": "MIT",
  "tags": [
   "eqesm:stage2",
   "model:atmosphere",
   "physics:deep-convection"
  ],
  "references": [
   {
    "citation": "Zhang, G. J. and McFarlane, N. A. (1995). Sensitivity of climate simulations to the parameterization of cumulus convection in the Canadian Climate Centre general circulation model. Atmosphere-Ocean 33(3), 407-446."
   },
   {
    "citation": "Raymond, D. J. and Blyth, A. M. (1992). Extension of the stochastic mixing model to cumulonimbus clouds. J. Atmos. Sci. 49, 1968-1983."
   }
  ]
 },
 "index_sets": {
  "lev": {
   "kind": "interval",
   "size": 32
  }
 },
